 "t07": {
  "verdict_reason": "The single predicate _token_ok is still a TOKEN-SHAPE proxy for content, and _pure_filler is still a SINGLE-TOKEN proxy. Both are beaten the same way the length heuristic was: a value whose tokens individually pass the shape rule, or a list entry that is not a single ascii word, validates while carrying nothing but filler. Fixing this round by adding shapes (vowel trigrams, repeated pairs, run-subsets) to the denylist cannot close it - the adversary only needs a token that is alphabetic, >=3, carries one vowel, is not one repeated character, is not a substring of a keyboard row/column, and is not on the denylist. 'banana phone banana', 'ababab', 'hahaha' and 'aei' all satisfy that and mean nothing.",
